From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: tunnel: drop domain reference when DPRX work is
 canceled

tb_tunnel_one_dp() passes tb_domain_get(tb) as @callback_data, and the
reference is dropped only by the callback (tb_dp_tunnel_active() ->
tb_domain_put()). When a DP tunnel is torn down before its DPRX work
runs, tb_dp_dprx_stop() cancels the work and drops only the tunnel
reference, so the callback never runs and the domain reference leaks.

On kernels that wait for nhi->domain_released in the PCI remove/shutdown
path (Ubuntu linux-oem-7.0 7.0.0-1015, carrying a v7.2-rc1 backport),
the leak turns into a permanent hang at shutdown/reboot. Reproduced on
HP ZBook Ultra G1a with a Belkin TB4 5-in-1 Core Hub (0x13:0x6e) whose
DP OUT adapter flaps right after plug-in: 4/4 shutdowns hung before,
clean shutdown after this change.

Only tb_tunnel_one_dp() passes a callback (test.c passes NULL), always
with a domain reference. If cancel fails the work is running and the
callback drops the reference itself, so there is no double put.

---
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/tunnel.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/tunnel.c
@@ -1136,8 +1136,20 @@
 	if (tunnel->dprx_started) {
 		tunnel->dprx_started = false;
 		tunnel->dprx_canceled = true;
-		if (cancel_delayed_work(&tunnel->dprx_work))
+		if (cancel_delayed_work(&tunnel->dprx_work)) {
+			/*
+			 * The work will not run, so neither will @callback, which is
+			 * what drops the domain reference tb_tunnel_one_dp() handed us
+			 * in @callback_data. Drop it here instead, otherwise the domain
+			 * never gets released and nhi_pci_shutdown() waits forever
+			 * (seen with a TB4 hub whose DP OUT adapter flaps on plug).
+			 * Only tb_tunnel_one_dp() passes a callback, always with a
+			 * domain reference.
+			 */
+			if (tunnel->callback)
+				tb_domain_put(tunnel->callback_data);
 			tb_tunnel_put(tunnel);
+		}
 	}
 }
 
